WEBVTT

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:06.030
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.610
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.410
The eight mighty trainers
aiming for the summit...

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.830
...have begun battling.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.540
The first round,
composed of 3v3 battles...

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.380
The second match was
Wataru versus Carne.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.420
Against Wataru’s advancing
dragon brigade,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:31.050
Carne skillfully used super effective attacks
and defensive moves to claim victory,

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.140
landing a seat in the semifinals.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.600
And now, the third match is the Champion of Sinnoh,
Shirona, versus the Champion of Isshu, Iris.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.110
This battle is a 3v3! Both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.070
Three!

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:47.940
Two!

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:48.820
One!

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.950
Go!

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.410
Come out, Doryuzu!

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.450
Emerge from the waves, Toritodon!

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:43.730
Toritodon! Sea Slug Pokémon!
Water/Ground type!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.400
Although its body is squishy,
it’s remarkably resilient!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:49.190
The softness of its body
helps absorb the force of impacts!

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.320
Doryuzu! Subterrene Pokémon!
Ground/Steel type!

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:56.110
Also known as the Drill King!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:01.080
It can tunnel through the terrain
at speeds reaching 150 km/h!

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:06.170
Iris has been raising that Doryuzu
since he was a Moguryu!

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.170
I haven’t seen him in so long...

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.380
What?! You know her too?!

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.050
You see, Iris adventured
around Isshu with Satoshi.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.220
He’s well acquainted
with Ms. Shirona, too.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:19.760
Wh-What’s up with you, Satoshi...?

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.890
We’re bursting with excitement!

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:24.020
It’s gonna be
squishy against steely!

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:25.440
I can’t wait, meow!

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.520
Snore, snore...

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.980
It went back to sleep!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.360
Huh?

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.190
What is it?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.490
Getting a good look at her,
I recognize that frilly girl, meow!

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.990
You’re right!
It’s the Isshu brat girl!

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.030
My, oh my,
she sure is all dressed up.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.880
But Iris is a Dragon user...

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.880
Doryuzu was quite the surprise.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.380
Apparently, she’s even had lessons
from Ms. Shirona.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.430
So both of them
know each other’s cards...

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.720
Will we get to see
a changing of the guard?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.640
This is one to watch!

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.270
Toritodon versus Doryuzu!

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.770
What sort of battle
is about to unfold?

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:16.030
Let the battle begin!

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.320
Toritodon!
Rain Prayer!

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.410
It started to rain!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.370
The power of Water-type moves
will increase!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.420
Doryuzu! Metal Claw!

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.960
Metal Claws
cleaving through the rain!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.970
Toritodon!
Take the blow!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.050
It connec—

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.180
Whoa! It repelled him!

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.640
I can tell you’ve
sharpened up your attacks!

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.310
You taught me a lot,
Ms. Shirona!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.520
Your advice from back then...

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:56.030
...is still helping us,
even now!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.280
Thanks to you,
I even became Champion!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.280
And today,
as the Champion of Isshu, Iris...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.290
Ms. Shirona,
I’m going to defeat you!

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.080
Toritodon,
use Muddy Water!

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:12.500
Focus Blast!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.470
Doryuzu!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.890
As we stand upon this stage...

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.770
We are both nothing more than
Pokémon Trainers!

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.440
Yet at the same time,
challengers aiming for the top!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.020
I won’t go easy on you.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.780
To test my own potential...

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.660
I shall defeat you
and move onward!

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:43.910
Toritodon! Dissolve!

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.200
Drill Liner!

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:02.470
Oh? Toritodon is completely unfazed
by the Drill Liner!

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:07.390
Of course, Dissolve is a move
that raises your Defense.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:10.770
Her Water-type moves
have been powered up with Rain Prayer, too.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.310
Ms. Shirona is ruthless!

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.440
What’s your attack plan, Iris?

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.400
Don’t worry, Doryuzu!

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.030
It’s our turn, Toritodon!

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.900
Muddy Water!

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.620
Doryuzu! Dodge it!

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:37.670
And Doryuzu is swallowed
by Toritodon’s Muddy Water once again!

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.930
I’ll put my faith in Doryuzu...

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.430
...and bet on this attack!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:53.940
Horn Drill!

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:04.400
One-hit... knockout!

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.630
Toritodon is unable to battle!

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:23.880
A one-hit knockout victory
from Doryuzu!

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:27.510
Competitor Shirona is the first one
to take a black mark.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.890
The Rain Prayer’s effect
has also ended.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.390
All right!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:35.270
Good going, Iris, Doryuzu!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.150
But she can’t let her guard down.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.270
She’s up against Ms. Shirona.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.110
You’re not half bad,
frilly Isshu girl.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:47.700
It’s thanks to all our training
that you made it this far, meow.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.450
You should come
thank us sometime.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.500
You did well, Toritodon.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.630
Spirit of water, show your elegance...
Milokaross!

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.640
Competitor Shirona
sends in Milokaross!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:17.180
Right now, Competitor Iris
is keeping up the pressure.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.640
What will she do next?

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:20.650
Rush in, Doryuzu!

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:21.770
Drill Liner!

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:25.820
Hydro Pump!

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:33.120
Hydro Pump hits its target!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.210
Doryuzu is unable to battle!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.510
Doryuzu...
You did good hanging in there.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.720
That incredible speed...

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.810
I couldn’t predict
how Milokaross would move!

00:08:55.810 --> 00:08:59.310
This time, Competitor Iris
takes the black mark!

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.060
Kairyu, I’m counting on you!

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.320
Ooh, I haven’t seen him in a while.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.450
Ms. Shirona, just watch and see
what Kairyu can do!

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.660
Thunder Punch!

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:25.090
An Electric move,
super effective against Water types!

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.090
That’s gotta sting!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.470
Charm Voice!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.940
A Fairy move!

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:44.150
They’re devastatingly effective
on Dragon types!

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.650
Kairyu, hold on!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.860
Milokaross!

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:54.990
Oh, no!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.370
Iron Head!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.170
Kairyu!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.010
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:19.350
Kairyu couldn’t stand up
to Milokaross’s rapid onslaught!

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:22.230
Competitor Iris
takes a second black mark!

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.940
She’s strong...

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.860
That Milokaross is terrifying...

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.150
Kairyu...
You must feel frustrated.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.820
The pain of my Pokémon...
I feel it, too!

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.620
Just wait and see.
I’ll win the next bout!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.080
Ononox...

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:42.870
It’s all up to you!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:52.050
There he is! Ononox!

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.840
He’s really strong!

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:56.140
I knew she’d pick him!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.010
But he’s a Dragon type...

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:01.930
How’s he supposed to handle
Milokaross’s Fairy moves?

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:03.520
Ms. Shirona!

00:11:04.270 --> 00:11:08.520
When I became the Champion,
he’s the one who finished the battle!

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:12.530
He’s always giving me strength!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.490
Milokaross! Charm Voice!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.370
Psycho Cutter!

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.460
Pretty good.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.220
All right!

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:37.180
So her approach is
“offense is the best defense”?

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.010
Looking good, Iris!

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.140
Wide Breaker!

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.770
Hydro Pump!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.150
Cutting through the Hydro Pump,
the Wide Breaker bursts forth!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:04.120
Milokaross is unable to battle!

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:07.750
That was so cool, Ononox!

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.000
You fought well,

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.340
Milokaross.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:19.390
Competitor Shirona is also left
with only one Pokémon.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:21.640
She’s got Ms. Shirona cornered!

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.140
Amazing...

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.720
Is it finally time for her ace?

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.690
Take to the skies...

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.900
Gaburias!

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.120
So you’re finally here,
Gaburias.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:43.870
You gotta keep your calm, Iris!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.580
Dragon versus dragon...

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:48.580
This is going to settle it.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:56.590
Competitor Shirona’s third Pokémon is her greatest partner,
whose countless battles have become legends... Gaburias!

00:12:57.090 --> 00:13:01.340
Now, how will Competitor Iris
and Ononox combat this?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.860
Shower upon us, stars of the heavens!
Draco Meteor!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:28.790
Reversed Scale!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.590
Ononox charges in without any care
for the Draco Meteor!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.800
Wow...
What a battle style!

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:46.350
Does nothing scare him?!

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.440
A fierce trade of blows!

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.070
But neither goes down!

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:11.160
Oh! Ononox has become confused
from Reversed Scale’s effect!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:21.970
What’s this? Ononox hit his own head
to snap out of the confusion!

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.800
Now <i>that’s</i> amazing!

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:27.100
I’ve never seen anything
like this before...

00:14:27.100 --> 00:14:29.770
That’s Iris’s brand of
crazy tactics!

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:32.810
Yeah! You can do this, Iris!

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.690
This isn’t over.
Nowhere close.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:38.730
We can still keep fighting!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:40.940
You are marvelous, Iris.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.070
Now, let’s do it! Ononox!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.530
Right.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:49.950
In that case...

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:56.960
I shall defeat you
with all my might!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:00.590
That’s...!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.090
...a Key Stone!

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.840
Gaburias...

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.680
Mega Evolve!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.870
Mega Gaburias!

00:15:30.870 --> 00:15:32.490
She’s so cool!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.000
Ms. Shirona
used Mega Evolution?!

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.960
I suppose this is
her showing she’s serious.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:42.380
However, Ononox has
a lot of potential, too.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:45.880
I can’t tell how the battle
will play out.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:48.260
That’s an incredible
hidden trick, meow.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.180
Now I’m getting fired up!

00:15:50.180 --> 00:15:51.310
How strong!

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:53.890
I want it! I <i>really</i> want it!

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.410
Dragon Claw!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.410
Ononox! Lure her in,
then use Psycho Cutter!

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:22.420
Tremendous power
collides with tremendous power!

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.550
<i>Attack!</i>

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.430
That Ononox is
putting up a real fight!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.940
Dragon Pulse!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:51.200
We’re almost there!

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:54.200
I’ll hone my mind...

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.250
...and become one
with my Pokémon!

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:09.930
Ononox.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.930
This is our final attack.

00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:16.890
Let’s give it
everything we’ve got!

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:27.110
Gaburias,
finish her with the next move.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.190
Draco Meteor!

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:36.580
Ononox!
Use Dragon Pulse!

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:40.060
Ononox is unable to battle!
Gaburias wins!

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:43.890
As such, the winner is
Competitor Shirona!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.900
It finally comes to an end!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:51.360
In the third match of the first round,
the referee’s fan rises for Competitor Shirona!

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:59.120
Gaburias...
You battled well.

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:00.240
Thank you.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.080
You did your best, Ononox.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:14.930
Ononox... Kairyu... Doryuzu...

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:16.300
I love all of you.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.600
Iris?

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.430
Ms. Shirona...

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:24.850
Thank you very much.

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:27.900
I’m going to get
a whole lot stronger.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.860
That was an unforgettable battle.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.980
You have my thanks, too.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.160
The frilly Isshu girl
was so close, meow!

00:19:40.160 --> 00:19:43.290
No, this loss will
only make her stronger!

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:45.120
I know it will!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:49.130
That’s right...
You can follow our example.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:57.380
That was a really amazing
Dragon showdown!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.470
Yeah...

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:00.720
Iris...

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.770
Hey, Satoshi?

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:10.650
And so, Competitor Shirona
secures her advancement to the semifinals!

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:14.440
The upcoming fourth match
will decide her opponent.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.450
Iris... Too bad, huh?

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.420
Satoshi...

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.590
I lost.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.340
You did, huh?

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:38.220
Ms. Shirona is so amazing!

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.220
She’s amazing...

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:47.180
Amazing, but...

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:05.660
Ah, now I feel better!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.330
Thank you.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:12.290
I know! For Satoshi’s next match,
let’s cheer him on together!

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:15.170
Yeah! Let’s!

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.010
I’m counting on you two, then!

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:25.260
The third match of the first round
in the Pokémon World Championships...

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.720
...has ended in Shirona’s victory.

00:21:28.270 --> 00:21:31.940
And now, Satoshi’s battle
is finally beginning.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.980
His opponent is
the Champion of Hoenn, Daigo.

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:41.110
How will Satoshi fight this mighty
opponent?

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:10.990
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.870
Next is the fourth match
of the first round!

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:18.380
The Champion of Hoenn, Competitor Daigo,
versus the Champion of Alola, Competitor Brat Boy, meow!

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:20.000
So, what should we
keep our eyes on?

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.300
Let’s see, it’d have to be...
My good looks, hmm?

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:23.840
Mr. Head Deluxe, go ahead!

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:26.930
The regional delicacies
that Morpeko’s always snacking on, meow!

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:28.220
You’re picking <i>that?!</i>

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:30.180
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:32.390
Satoshi Heads Into Battle! VS Daigo!!

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:34.180
Let’s all tune in, meow!
